// Layout canary: two instantiations of ONE generic struct in one program must
// NOT share a layout. Values are deliberately asymmetric — 1000000 does not fit
// t8, so a shared or last-wins t8 layout truncates it, and a shared t64 layout
// misreads the t8 one. Symmetric values would mask exactly this.
struct Box<T> { v: T }
s: Box = Box<t8> { v: 7 }
w: Box = Box<t64> { v: 1000000 }
print(s.v)
print(w.v)
